    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (65.38) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) headlining our offensive strategy. **Junior Caminero** occupies the optimal #2 spot, and despite the daunting 3.72 xERA of Gausman, his dynamic platoon splits and superior barrel rate keep him firmly in \"Strong\" territory. Meanwhile, **Casey Schmitt** represents our highest-value play, benefiting from a massive boost against the 5.30 xERA of Sasaki. With **Casey Schmitt** batting third and carrying an 11% platoon-driven efficiency bump, he is projected to provide the best ROI for our Roto categories today. **Yordan Alvarez** (60.94) remains a staple in the lineup, as his elite 0.429 xwOBA helps mitigate the risks posed by Kirby\u2019s 3.50 xERA.\n\nDown the roster, the bench remains thin due to scheduled off-days for **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Kyle Schwarber**, while **Christian Yelich** remains sidelined on the IL. With no primary speed threats available to chase stolen bases\u2014our most critical scarcity\u2014we are forced to prioritize contact and power profiles today. **Luke Raley** (52.77) makes the cut over other depth options like **Lars Nootbaar** or **Josh Smith** because his profile against Lambert provides the most stable floor for counting stats. **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.31) and **Hyeseong Kim** (40.48) are lower-confidence starts today; **Hyeseong Kim** specifically suffers from a tough matchup against a 2.60 xERA arm and a suboptimal #9 spot in the order, but his inclusion is necessary to ensure we reach our daily game caps. We are monitoring the lineups for **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, and **Carson Benge** closely, as any positive late-breaking news regarding their order placement could force a pivot from our current fringe starters.",
